### Register normal user
POST {{ApiGateway_HostAddress}}/api/accounts/register?role=User
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "user1@example.com",
  "password": "P@ssw0rd123!",
  "phone": "1234567890",
  "name": "hello"
}

### Register staff user
POST {{ApiGateway_HostAddress}}/api/accounts/register?role=Staff
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "staff1@example.com",
  "password": "P@ssw0rd123!",
  "phone": "1234567890"
}

### Login
POST {{ApiGateway_HostAddress}}/api/accounts/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "user1@example.com",
  "password": "P@ssw0rd123!"
}

### Me
GET {{ApiGateway_HostAddress}}/api/accounts/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### Call downstream THROUGH gateway (claims injected)
GET {{ApiGateway_HostAddress}}/api/service1s/api/secure/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### Call a role-protected downstream endpoint (expects User role)
GET {{ApiGateway_HostAddress}}/api/service1s/api/secure/staff-area
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### (Negative test) Direct call to downstream (should fail 401 because no headers)
GET https://localhost:7101/api/secure/me
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### (Optional) Same direct call with forged headers (should be blocked by network, not code)
# 2 see current exposure; secure via network/mTLS/firewall.
GET https://localhost:7101/api/secure/me
X-User-Id: some-user-id
X-User-Role: Staff
Accept: application/json